1
00:01:38,508 --> 00:01:40,343
Let’s start from the beginning.

2
00:01:40,945 --> 00:01:41,737
Hi.

3
00:01:43,763 --> 00:01:45,890
I’m Shan. Nice to meet you.

4
00:01:46,933 --> 00:01:47,892
Hello!

5
00:01:47,892 --> 00:01:51,229
I prepared some
topics we could explore.

6
00:01:54,274 --> 00:01:56,693
Is there something
that’s making you happy?

7
00:01:58,278 --> 00:01:59,154
Or…

8
00:01:59,266 --> 00:02:00,684
Or is it someone?

9
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:03,045
I really enjoyed everything we did.

10
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:05,035
Are there still a lot on the list?

11
00:02:05,035 --> 00:02:08,496
Let’s start making your
yesterdays happy, starting today.

12
00:02:11,541 --> 00:02:13,335
I’m so proud of you, Ke.

13
00:02:13,856 --> 00:02:19,330
You’re still the loving person that you
are, and you extend that love to others.

14
00:02:20,842 --> 00:02:23,428
You did not betray yourself, Kierra.

15
00:02:25,013 --> 00:02:26,431
He betrayed you.

16
00:02:26,931 --> 00:02:27,891
I already told you!

17
00:02:28,933 --> 00:02:29,726
You’re not listening.

18
00:02:29,726 --> 00:02:31,102
I already told you, didn’t I?

19
00:02:31,102 --> 00:02:32,479
Didn’t I just tell you a minute ago?

20
00:02:32,479 --> 00:02:33,772
Why aren’t you listening, huh?

21
00:02:33,797 --> 00:02:35,799
Answer me. Answer!

22
00:04:13,001 --> 00:04:13,961
Can you just leave
me alone, Miguel?

23
00:04:14,002 --> 00:04:15,129
I haven’t slept yet.

24
00:04:15,889 --> 00:04:18,559
I just want to know one thing, bro.
What do you know about me?

25
00:04:18,584 --> 00:04:20,002
What are you so afraid of?

26
00:04:21,677 --> 00:04:23,804
You mentioned Kierra. Why?

27
00:04:26,102 --> 00:04:27,437
So you do know her.

28
00:04:27,603 --> 00:04:29,272
Why did you pretend you didn’t?

29
00:04:29,853 --> 00:04:31,646
I didn’t pretend.

30
00:04:32,108 --> 00:04:33,818
She’s just not…

31
00:04:34,777 --> 00:04:37,405
that important for
me to remember her.

32
00:04:38,614 --> 00:04:42,201
Why? Is she saying something?
Is she talking to people?

33
00:04:42,548 --> 00:04:45,301
Dude, if I were you, I’d stay
away from her, you know why?

34
00:04:46,247 --> 00:04:48,041
She’s still crazy.

35
00:04:48,041 --> 00:04:49,042
Shut up.

36
00:04:50,084 --> 00:04:52,003
Unless something’s
going on between you two?

37
00:04:52,003 --> 00:04:52,962
Is there?

38
00:04:53,379 --> 00:04:56,382
‘Cause dude, I’m telling you,
she almost ruined my life.

39
00:04:56,549 --> 00:04:59,969
She would spread rumors about me.
She could do that to you.

40
00:05:00,011 --> 00:05:01,387
You want to be a lawyer, right?

41
00:05:01,512 --> 00:05:03,514
What if your reputation gets
ruined? ​​Then think about me.

42
00:05:03,639 --> 00:05:04,974
You know she sleeps around,
she sleeps around.

43
00:05:04,974 --> 00:05:07,268
She’d do anything, I’m telling you.

44
00:05:07,268 --> 00:05:09,187
Absolutely anything just
to get what she wants.

45
00:05:09,437 --> 00:05:10,355
She’s sick in the head.

46
00:05:10,355 --> 00:05:12,273
I heard she’s seeing a doctor.

47
00:05:12,315 --> 00:05:14,359
And who does that? Sick people.

48
00:05:14,359 --> 00:05:15,151
Like Kierra.

49
00:05:15,151 --> 00:05:16,736
She’s pretty, but she’s crazy.

50
00:05:16,903 --> 00:05:17,779
Dude, she’s kind of crazy—

51
00:05:17,779 --> 00:05:19,030
I said shut up!

52
00:05:26,704 --> 00:05:28,122
I’m just worried about you, man.

53
00:05:29,819 --> 00:05:30,743
Chill.

54
00:05:30,917 --> 00:05:31,709
Chill.

55
00:05:35,546 --> 00:05:37,757
I’m just telling you ‘cause women like her—

56
00:05:38,841 --> 00:05:40,968
like Kierra? She’s pretty.

57
00:05:42,261 --> 00:05:43,805
But she’s nothing but a headache.

58
00:05:44,722 --> 00:05:45,765
Not worth it.

59
00:05:46,182 --> 00:05:47,517
Pain in the ass.

60
00:05:51,437 --> 00:05:52,855
Don’t say I didn’t tell you.

61
00:05:53,106 --> 00:05:54,357
I promise you.

62
00:05:54,565 --> 00:05:55,608
Crazy.

63
00:05:56,916 --> 00:05:58,319
Crazy!

64
00:06:00,113 --> 00:06:01,322
Cuckoo.

65
00:06:16,187 --> 00:06:17,730
You’re done. You’re done, bro.

66
00:06:17,755 --> 00:06:19,632
- Damn!
- It’s over, bro.

67
00:06:21,634 --> 00:06:22,885
Who hurt you, bro?

68
00:06:24,137 --> 00:06:25,638
Some fucking asshole.

69
00:06:26,264 --> 00:06:28,474
If I end up becoming a criminal
because of that asshole…

70
00:06:29,613 --> 00:06:30,739
I’ll bail you out.

71
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:33,672
Even if it’s a violent crime?

72
00:06:35,273 --> 00:06:36,023
Why?

73
00:06:36,357 --> 00:06:37,900
You want to commit murder?

74
00:06:38,401 --> 00:06:40,653
Who is he? What did he do?

75
00:06:41,904 --> 00:06:42,738
Wait.

76
00:06:45,158 --> 00:06:47,452
Don’t tell me you’re
studying law to break it.

77
00:06:49,495 --> 00:06:50,538
It’s not me.

78
00:06:51,622 --> 00:06:52,707
I just know someone.

79
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,169
You know, it really
pisses me off sometimes.

80
00:06:56,752 --> 00:07:00,631
How can they be in law school,
studying everything about the law,

81
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:03,301
and still break it so easily?

82
00:07:04,343 --> 00:07:07,889
They’re heartless, no conscience at all.

83
00:07:08,598 --> 00:07:14,562
Let me guess, that someone
has money and power.

84
00:07:15,646 --> 00:07:21,402
Well, people like that
don’t fear doing evil.

85
00:07:23,654 --> 00:07:26,741
They fear losing control.

86
00:07:36,931 --> 00:07:38,918
<i>Ciandrei! Are we still on for tomorrow?</i>

87
00:07:38,943 --> 00:07:39,860
<i> Also...</i>

88
00:07:41,255 --> 00:07:43,549
<i>Look! I made myself coffee.</i>

89
00:07:46,260 --> 00:07:47,929
<i>It’s better than yours!</i>

90
00:07:48,846 --> 00:07:54,185
<i>Yup. Still on for tomorrow. I’ll fetch</i>
<i>you lunch time. Let’s eat somewhere first.</i>

91
00:07:54,393 --> 00:07:58,314
<i>Let me taste that coffee and</i>
<i>see if it’s really better than mine.</i>

92
00:08:04,468 --> 00:08:08,264
<i>That’ll cost you. You think you get</i>
<i>a free taste? I actually pay at your cafe!</i>

93
00:08:08,615 --> 00:08:12,244
<i>How about... my kiss as payment?</i>

94
00:08:15,373 --> 00:08:19,043
<i>Nope, no thanks. Your
kiss can’t pay for the bills.</i>

95
00:08:22,463 --> 00:08:24,173
Your mood changed so fast.

96
00:08:26,551 --> 00:08:27,718
That is different, bro.

97
00:08:31,180 --> 00:08:32,640
Shut up.

98
00:08:36,185 --> 00:08:37,436
Go ahead and try to beat me.

99
00:08:37,603 --> 00:08:38,646
Sure.

100
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:52,410
Here it is.

101
00:09:00,918 --> 00:09:03,129
Hi, Auntie. I’m Kierra.

102
00:09:03,629 --> 00:09:05,256
I’m Shan’s friend.

103
00:09:05,798 --> 00:09:08,426
We met before when I was little.

104
00:09:10,052 --> 00:09:13,014
Look at me now. All grown up.

105
00:09:17,143 --> 00:09:19,562
Hey, why are you just standing there?

106
00:09:20,438 --> 00:09:22,648
Aren’t you going to talk to your mom?

107
00:09:24,317 --> 00:09:25,276
No.

108
00:09:26,485 --> 00:09:29,196
It’s okay. She can’t hear you anyway.

109
00:09:30,239 --> 00:09:32,074
Who knows, maybe she can.

110
00:09:33,075 --> 00:09:36,245
Don’t you talk to her when you visit?

111
00:09:40,354 --> 00:09:41,564
Okay, I’ll do it.

112
00:09:41,751 --> 00:09:43,336
Hi again, Auntie.

113
00:09:45,046 --> 00:09:47,923
I’m here with your son, Ciandrei.

114
00:09:48,249 --> 00:09:51,461
He won’t talk, though.
He’s probably shy.

115
00:09:55,598 --> 00:09:58,851
You know, you don’t have to talk to Mom.

116
00:09:59,644 --> 00:10:01,771
You better be careful, she might
actually answer you someday.

117
00:10:02,396 --> 00:10:06,067
Ah, so that’s why you
don’t want to talk to Auntie.

118
00:10:06,067 --> 00:10:09,153
You’re scared she’ll answer back, huh?

119
00:10:09,445 --> 00:10:12,239
Oh my, Auntie, your son is such a coward.

120
00:10:13,282 --> 00:10:14,533
No way.

121
00:10:14,867 --> 00:10:17,078
Besides, Mom wouldn’t believe you anyway.

122
00:10:17,370 --> 00:10:19,914
She knows how brave I was as a kid.

123
00:10:20,289 --> 00:10:22,208
I even took up martial arts.

124
00:10:22,208 --> 00:10:26,170
Because she wanted me to be able to protect
myself and the people who matter to me.

125
00:10:27,755 --> 00:10:30,591
And what can your martial
arts do against a ghost?

126
00:10:37,014 --> 00:10:37,932
Are you okay?

127
00:10:38,224 --> 00:10:38,974
Yeah.

128
00:10:38,974 --> 00:10:40,184
You look pale.

129
00:10:40,518 --> 00:10:44,230
No, I’m fine. I’m just a little
sleep-deprived, but I’m okay.

130
00:10:45,940 --> 00:10:46,565
Oh.

131
00:10:47,149 --> 00:10:48,901
Wait, I have to take this.

132
00:10:49,527 --> 00:10:50,486
Auntie, I’ll be right back.

133
00:11:20,891 --> 00:11:22,184
Hi, Mom.

134
00:11:25,438 --> 00:11:26,566
You remember Kierra, right?

135
00:11:33,195 --> 00:11:34,324
That’s her now.

136
00:11:35,614 --> 00:11:36,628
We’re together now.

137
00:11:39,118 --> 00:11:42,042
We’re doing our best to be happy.

138
00:11:45,319 --> 00:11:50,199
Hopefully, soon, we’ll really be happy.

139
00:12:04,310 --> 00:12:05,503
And be free as well.

140
00:12:24,330 --> 00:12:26,415
Hey, you’ve been coughing this whole time.

141
00:12:26,415 --> 00:12:28,125
- Sorry.
- Are you sure you’re okay?

142
00:12:28,501 --> 00:12:29,794
Yeah, yeah. I’m good.

143
00:12:33,005 --> 00:12:34,590
You’re running a fever now.

144
00:12:35,424 --> 00:12:36,425
No, I’m not.

145
00:12:36,653 --> 00:12:37,694
What are you, a thermometer?

146
00:12:37,718 --> 00:12:38,677
Why?

147
00:12:39,261 --> 00:12:40,679
That wasn’t a pick-up line.

148
00:12:40,679 --> 00:12:42,264
I’m serious.

149
00:12:42,264 --> 00:12:45,768
You’re all alone in your condo.
Can you really take care of yourself?

150
00:12:47,269 --> 00:12:48,771
I’m not going to die, Kierra.

151
00:12:50,314 --> 00:12:51,774
Can you still drive?

152
00:12:51,774 --> 00:12:53,692
Do you want to stay at our condo for a bit?

153
00:12:57,172 --> 00:12:58,331
Sorry.

154
00:12:58,864 --> 00:13:01,158
Is it okay if we switch for now?

155
00:13:01,158 --> 00:13:04,286
Of course, I’ll drive. We can
switch at the gas station.

156
00:13:05,287 --> 00:13:06,205
Are you sure?

157
00:13:06,925 --> 00:13:07,706
Okay.

158
00:13:07,873 --> 00:13:08,749
Thank you.

159
00:13:20,886 --> 00:13:22,513
Ke! You’re home—

160
00:13:25,558 --> 00:13:27,142
with a guy.

161
00:13:27,402 --> 00:13:30,145
Ciandrei’s going to rest
here for now. He’s sick.

162
00:13:30,896 --> 00:13:32,147
What is this, a clinic?

163
00:13:32,773 --> 00:13:33,649
Hi, Luna.

164
00:13:34,316 --> 00:13:35,484
Don’t you “Hi, Luna” me.

165
00:13:35,693 --> 00:13:37,236
Do you have a big T-shirt?

166
00:13:37,236 --> 00:13:39,280
Ciandrei’s drenched in sweat, poor guy.

167
00:13:39,363 --> 00:13:41,866
I don’t care if that Sunday guy
is drenched in sweat.

168
00:13:45,327 --> 00:13:47,121
I think she’s pissed at me.

169
00:13:47,580 --> 00:13:50,666
No. She’s always like that,
but she’s fine with you being here.

170
00:13:54,753 --> 00:13:55,421
Here.

171
00:13:57,840 --> 00:13:58,966
Here are the meds.

172
00:14:02,928 --> 00:14:04,138
How’d you get this shirt?

173
00:14:04,555 --> 00:14:05,764
From her ex, Kalix.

174
00:14:07,391 --> 00:14:08,434
Kalix?

175
00:14:09,059 --> 00:14:11,770
Kalix Martinez? I know him.

176
00:14:12,521 --> 00:14:14,273
Well, congrats, you know my ex.

177
00:14:15,024 --> 00:14:17,192
Oh, so you two dated.

178
00:14:18,203 --> 00:14:19,538
Why did you two break up?

179
00:14:19,737 --> 00:14:23,115
I thought you were sick,
so why are you gossiping?

180
00:14:23,324 --> 00:14:25,618
Ke, shut him up.
Or I’m kicking him out.

181
00:14:25,618 --> 00:14:27,536
Just don’t comment about Kalix anymore.

182
00:14:27,536 --> 00:14:29,538
So, are you hungry?
Want me to cook for you?

183
00:14:53,354 --> 00:14:54,480
It’s good.

184
00:14:55,981 --> 00:14:57,650
I feel like I’m getting better.

185
00:14:58,567 --> 00:14:59,526
Pay up.

186
00:14:59,735 --> 00:15:01,487
My services aren’t free.

187
00:15:19,338 --> 00:15:20,172
My payment.

188
00:15:25,135 --> 00:15:27,805
Unlimited coffee. Really?

189
00:15:27,856 --> 00:15:29,983
If your cafe goes bankrupt,
you can’t blame me, okay?

190
00:15:31,809 --> 00:15:34,728
Why do you love sticky notes
so much? You always carry them.

191
00:15:35,729 --> 00:15:40,401
When I was little, it was
hard for me to communicate.

192
00:15:41,318 --> 00:15:44,530
There were things I couldn’t tell Mom,
so she gave me sticky notes

193
00:15:44,530 --> 00:15:46,991
to write down what I wanted to say.

194
00:15:47,950 --> 00:15:49,493
Why couldn’t you tell your mom?

195
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:56,458
Whenever I cried back then,
it was because of Dad.

196
00:15:58,252 --> 00:16:03,424
But even with sticky notes, I couldn’t
tell her what Dad was doing.

197
00:16:04,383 --> 00:16:09,013
Sometimes I’d write
“I’m fine, Mommy,” even when I wasn’t.

198
00:16:09,972 --> 00:16:12,182
Or if I really couldn’t take it anymore,

199
00:16:12,558 --> 00:16:16,228
I’d write “I want to stay in school,
Mommy,” just so I could get away from Dad.

200
00:16:35,998 --> 00:16:39,084
Ke, are you hungry?
Let me cook for you.

201
00:16:39,084 --> 00:16:39,918
Mhmm.

202
00:16:41,462 --> 00:16:42,671
I can cook. Is that okay?

203
00:16:42,671 --> 00:16:45,466
Huh? You’re not allowed
to use our kitchen.

204
00:16:45,799 --> 00:16:48,260
Also, hello, Ke likes my cooking, right?

205
00:16:48,260 --> 00:16:49,261
Yeah.

206
00:16:49,845 --> 00:16:50,846
Do you?

207
00:16:51,680 --> 00:16:55,559
Wow, Shondei, you still doubt it?

208
00:16:55,601 --> 00:16:57,728
Luna, it’s Ciandrei.

209
00:16:57,728 --> 00:16:59,563
Also, can you two please stop fighting?

210
00:16:59,563 --> 00:17:01,899
I made soup, so that’s
what I’m going to eat.

211
00:17:04,651 --> 00:17:07,237
Oh, and that... that shirt.
Don’t give it back to me.

212
00:17:07,237 --> 00:17:08,864
It’s all yours.

213
00:17:09,573 --> 00:17:12,284
Yeah, sure. I’ll just
give it back to Kalix.

214
00:17:17,039 --> 00:17:18,207
Ke, stop me.

215
00:17:18,707 --> 00:17:20,084
Stop me.

216
00:17:20,084 --> 00:17:21,085
Yeah—

217
00:17:21,085 --> 00:17:23,462
You’re really taunting me…

218
00:17:26,465 --> 00:17:28,675
I can tell your cousin cherishes you.

219
00:17:29,718 --> 00:17:32,971
She just worries about me
when it comes to the guys I date.

220
00:17:33,514 --> 00:17:36,892
You know my last one, right?

221
00:18:29,945 --> 00:18:30,946
Cute.

222
00:19:11,653 --> 00:19:14,323
Who said you could use our kitchen?

223
00:19:15,866 --> 00:19:18,994
You’re just mad because
I beat you to cooking for Kierra.

224
00:19:19,661 --> 00:19:22,247
She will discover that my cooking
is better than yours, won't she?

225
00:19:23,624 --> 00:19:27,544
Wow, you’re already bothering me
first thing in the morning.

226
00:19:27,878 --> 00:19:28,754
Amazing.

227
00:19:29,087 --> 00:19:30,130
So, why?

228
00:19:31,381 --> 00:19:32,424
Why what?

229
00:19:32,841 --> 00:19:34,479
Why did you and Kalix break up?

230
00:19:35,802 --> 00:19:38,472
It’s a long story.
I had no idea you liked to gossip.

231
00:19:39,431 --> 00:19:42,976
I’m just curious to know
how you ended up with his shirt.

232
00:19:43,894 --> 00:19:45,103
Does he sleep here, too?

233
00:19:45,229 --> 00:19:49,066
Yes, yes, he sleep here.
Happy now?

234
00:19:49,650 --> 00:19:51,777
Fine, I’ll just take this. It looks good.

235
00:19:53,111 --> 00:19:54,071
- Oh.
- Don’t touch that.

236
00:19:54,071 --> 00:19:54,696
Why?

237
00:19:56,823 --> 00:19:57,824
That’s Kierra’s.

238
00:20:11,296 --> 00:20:13,006
No nightmares last night.

239
00:20:20,722 --> 00:20:22,891
<i>Smile today.</i>

240
00:20:37,322 --> 00:20:38,573
What’s up, Kalix?

241
00:20:40,492 --> 00:20:41,378
For you.

242
00:20:42,536 --> 00:20:43,370
What’s this?

243
00:20:43,870 --> 00:20:45,080
Go check it out yourself.

244
00:20:57,092 --> 00:20:58,343
And who gave you that?

245
00:20:58,802 --> 00:20:59,720
Luna.

246
00:21:01,471 --> 00:21:02,556
She lent it to me.

247
00:21:04,099 --> 00:21:05,600
Okay. You’re together now.

248
00:21:07,102 --> 00:21:08,603
Didn’t she kiss you before?

249
00:21:10,564 --> 00:21:11,732
Yeah, she did. But—

250
00:21:12,566 --> 00:21:16,987
Bro, sorry about last time.
I didn’t know you were into her.

251
00:21:17,654 --> 00:21:18,613
But…

252
00:21:19,706 --> 00:21:20,707
Luna and I aren’t a thing.

253
00:21:23,076 --> 00:21:24,119
I’m with her cousin.

254
00:21:26,121 --> 00:21:27,372
You mean, Kierra?

255
00:21:30,751 --> 00:21:32,502
How is she? Is she okay?

256
00:21:33,628 --> 00:21:36,798
Of course, they can’t be separated.
But yeah, she’s doing okay.

257
00:21:39,676 --> 00:21:40,761
Do you know Miguel?

258
00:21:44,973 --> 00:21:45,766
I know him.

259
00:21:46,808 --> 00:21:48,393
He’s my classmate in law school.

260
00:21:49,227 --> 00:21:52,105
So I know a little bit about
what happened between him and Kierra.

261
00:21:53,982 --> 00:21:55,400
You’re telling me that—

262
00:21:56,151 --> 00:21:59,029
that asshole had the audacity
to go to law school?

263
00:22:00,572 --> 00:22:01,573
I know.

264
00:22:02,991 --> 00:22:04,659
Look, just take care of her.

265
00:22:06,787 --> 00:22:08,747
She’s been through a lot, you know.

266
00:22:10,082 --> 00:22:11,124
You know what,

267
00:22:12,834 --> 00:22:14,628
you said the same thing Luna did.

268
00:22:15,837 --> 00:22:18,673
Actually, you and Luna are pretty alike.

269
00:22:20,967 --> 00:22:22,052
We’re not.

270
00:22:27,933 --> 00:22:30,227
Kalix, do you still love her?

271
00:22:32,062 --> 00:22:33,188
We’re over.

272
00:22:34,523 --> 00:22:36,274
That didn’t answer my question.

273
00:22:53,250 --> 00:22:54,292
Safe skies, bro.

274
00:22:55,085 --> 00:22:55,919
Thanks, Shan.

275
00:22:56,503 --> 00:22:58,338
He actually didn’t bring much stuff.

276
00:22:58,839 --> 00:23:02,342
Well, most of my
clothes are still in my unit.

277
00:23:02,884 --> 00:23:05,720
Well, he still hopes to get back together
with someone here in the Philippines.

278
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:07,681
That’s why he didn’t bring everything.

279
00:23:08,043 --> 00:23:09,502
Fuck off, Haze.

280
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:13,415
By the way, Shan, this is why I dropped by.

281
00:23:13,478 --> 00:23:16,314
This is my donation for Sam’s charity.

282
00:23:17,399 --> 00:23:19,526
Thanks, bro. There’s a lot here.

283
00:23:21,319 --> 00:23:22,863
Oh…

284
00:23:24,114 --> 00:23:25,365
Those kinds of toys.

285
00:23:26,867 --> 00:23:27,806
Why?

286
00:23:27,993 --> 00:23:29,196
What did you bring?

287
00:23:36,933 --> 00:23:38,226
The fuck, Haze!

288
00:23:39,421 --> 00:23:40,755
It’s supposed to be for kids!

289
00:23:41,089 --> 00:23:43,300
Well, you didn’t specify what kind of toys.

290
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:45,719
You’re such an idiot,
Haze. Are you serious?

291
00:23:46,052 --> 00:23:46,803
Do you actually use that stuff?

292
00:23:47,071 --> 00:23:47,846
Hell no!

293
00:23:47,846 --> 00:23:50,182
Well, I haven’t tried it.

294
00:23:50,223 --> 00:23:52,434
So these aren’t allowed?

295
00:23:52,976 --> 00:23:53,894
- No!
- No!

296
00:23:55,020 --> 00:23:56,104
Fine, just keep it then.

297
00:23:56,104 --> 00:23:57,439
Why me?

298
00:23:57,731 --> 00:23:59,649
I don’t—
Do I look like I use that stuff?

299
00:23:59,900 --> 00:24:00,837
Do you want it?

300
00:24:01,234 --> 00:24:01,985
Haze.

301
00:24:01,985 --> 00:24:05,614
Try it out.
It looks like you’ve had it for a while.

302
00:24:10,368 --> 00:24:14,372
Ke, can we please go drinking after this?

303
00:24:14,372 --> 00:24:16,845
Drinking again? No way!

304
00:24:17,334 --> 00:24:19,085
You’re being such a KJ.

305
00:24:19,878 --> 00:24:21,129
Kalix Jace.

306
00:24:21,880 --> 00:24:23,590
The fuck.

307
00:24:30,889 --> 00:24:31,598
Hi!

308
00:24:31,848 --> 00:24:32,641
Hi.

309
00:24:33,503 --> 00:24:35,243
Wow, that’s a lot. Come in.

310
00:24:35,268 --> 00:24:36,102
Put it over here.

311
00:24:41,942 --> 00:24:43,652
You’re here again, Shondei.

312
00:24:44,236 --> 00:24:46,738
Maybe you should start paying
rent, since you’re always here.

313
00:24:47,614 --> 00:24:48,573
Hi, Luna.

314
00:24:50,158 --> 00:24:52,369
You look stressed. Boy problems?

315
00:24:52,702 --> 00:24:54,913
Do I look stressed? Look at you.

316
00:24:55,372 --> 00:24:58,708
Kierra doesn’t want to drink with me,
not even here in the condo.

317
00:24:58,959 --> 00:25:01,211
You know what, how
about we drink instead?

318
00:25:01,836 --> 00:25:02,754
Sure, game!

319
00:25:03,004 --> 00:25:04,506
What drinks do you want?
Let’s order delivery.

320
00:25:04,756 --> 00:25:05,564
Yes!

321
00:25:06,091 --> 00:25:08,176
Good thing you’re not
a KJ like that one.

322
00:25:09,010 --> 00:25:10,011
Kalix Jace?

323
00:25:13,306 --> 00:25:16,142
Damn it, you two. Fuck you,
you deserve each other.

324
00:25:16,226 --> 00:25:18,520
Order already, or I’m
really gonna beat you up.

325
00:25:18,520 --> 00:25:19,729
Order now!

326
00:25:21,674 --> 00:25:22,842
Can I borrow your phone?

327
00:25:24,192 --> 00:25:26,695
Okay, you two go ahead and
drink. I’m just going to get something.

328
00:25:26,695 --> 00:25:27,634
Okay.

329
00:25:28,989 --> 00:25:30,824
You order, I’ll just pay you back.

330
00:25:37,038 --> 00:25:38,290
Cheers!

331
00:25:44,212 --> 00:25:45,213
Want some?

332
00:25:45,839 --> 00:25:48,174
I don’t want that, weak shit.

333
00:25:48,174 --> 00:25:49,050
Jeez!

334
00:25:49,593 --> 00:25:50,927
One more, one more.

335
00:25:52,429 --> 00:25:54,889
- What are you two drinking?
- Hey, come over here.

336
00:25:55,640 --> 00:25:56,516
There’s beer.

337
00:25:56,725 --> 00:25:57,601
Come on, join us.

338
00:25:57,601 --> 00:25:58,977
- Just one bottle.
- Hurry, cheers!

339
00:25:59,394 --> 00:26:00,687
Cheers!

340
00:26:01,313 --> 00:26:02,647
Toasting again—

341
00:26:08,028 --> 00:26:11,865
What did you end up doing
with the... with the shirt?

342
00:26:12,741 --> 00:26:13,700
I told you.

343
00:26:13,700 --> 00:26:14,284
What?

344
00:26:14,284 --> 00:26:15,493
I gave it back to Kalix.

345
00:26:16,202 --> 00:26:18,830
No, you didn’t! Tell me the truth.

346
00:26:19,205 --> 00:26:20,206
I’m serious.

347
00:26:20,624 --> 00:26:21,416
As if.

348
00:26:22,667 --> 00:26:24,127
I really did give it back to him.

349
00:26:24,127 --> 00:26:26,921
We met at a party, and I told
that it was you who returned it.

350
00:26:28,632 --> 00:26:29,799
Jerk, you actually said that?

351
00:26:29,799 --> 00:26:30,383
Mhmm.

352
00:26:31,426 --> 00:26:33,253
You told him that I told you to?

353
00:26:33,298 --> 00:26:37,093
I didn’t say that;
you’re an idiot, Shondei!

354
00:26:38,266 --> 00:26:41,227
You know, Luna, he says he still loves you.

355
00:26:41,227 --> 00:26:42,604
As if.

356
00:26:42,604 --> 00:26:43,855
He loves me?

357
00:26:44,397 --> 00:26:46,232
Fuck, no way.

358
00:26:46,441 --> 00:26:49,569
He doesn’t love me, fuck—

359
00:26:49,718 --> 00:26:51,762
Fuck! He loves me?

360
00:26:52,155 --> 00:26:52,989
Mhmm.

361
00:26:53,014 --> 00:26:55,517
He said, “I still love her, bro.”

362
00:26:56,201 --> 00:26:57,702
As if!

363
00:26:58,411 --> 00:27:00,580
Don't make me believe in those things.

364
00:27:00,580 --> 00:27:01,597
It’s true.

365
00:27:03,291 --> 00:27:05,832
I’m over it. He never
really loved me anyway.

366
00:27:08,838 --> 00:27:12,926
Did he love me?
He traded me for Amethyst, you know?

367
00:27:15,595 --> 00:27:18,723
I should be happy now,
since he’s happy, right?

368
00:27:18,723 --> 00:27:19,933
Besides, he loves—

369
00:27:19,933 --> 00:27:23,311
Fuck him. That jerk.

370
00:27:26,225 --> 00:27:28,102
He replaced me!

371
00:27:30,694 --> 00:27:32,237
No, no, I’m fine now.

372
00:27:32,779 --> 00:27:34,447
I’m fine.

373
00:27:34,906 --> 00:27:37,367
Right, Ke? I’m fine.
I’m gorgeous, after all.

374
00:27:37,367 --> 00:27:39,536
- Okay.
- Yeah.

375
00:27:41,621 --> 00:27:43,123
Fuck you, Shan!

376
00:27:44,249 --> 00:27:46,251
Now I’m reminded of Kalix.

377
00:27:55,635 --> 00:27:57,178
Turns out you’re a lightweight, Luna.

378
00:27:58,513 --> 00:28:00,682
I’m not drinking with you next time.

379
00:28:01,391 --> 00:28:03,017
You’re just a heavy drinker.

380
00:28:03,017 --> 00:28:04,394
Look, she’s about to fall asleep.

381
00:28:06,062 --> 00:28:07,480
Help me, let’s move her to the couch.

382
00:28:07,480 --> 00:28:08,386
Luna.

383
00:28:09,107 --> 00:28:09,774
Luna.

384
00:28:10,400 --> 00:28:10,942
Wake up!

385
00:28:11,526 --> 00:28:12,068
Hey!

386
00:28:12,068 --> 00:28:13,319
- He said he still loves you.
- Come on now.

387
00:28:13,319 --> 00:28:14,904
No. I don’t love him anymore.

388
00:28:15,196 --> 00:28:16,281
He’s the only one who’ll ever love you.

389
00:28:18,450 --> 00:28:19,743
Yeah. I’ll give you one.

390
00:28:19,951 --> 00:28:20,577
In your dreams.

391
00:28:20,577 --> 00:28:21,578
- That’s mine.
- Hurry, hurry.

392
00:28:21,578 --> 00:28:23,246
That’s mine, don’t you dare take it.

393
00:28:23,246 --> 00:28:23,955
Come on.

394
00:28:23,955 --> 00:28:24,998
Come on now.

395
00:28:24,998 --> 00:28:25,999
Come on, over here.

396
00:28:28,668 --> 00:28:29,519
There.

397
00:28:30,044 --> 00:28:31,713
Okay, okay…

398
00:28:37,093 --> 00:28:39,220
I told you she’d fall asleep right away.

399
00:28:39,220 --> 00:28:41,723
I thought you still wanted
more, but you’re a lightweight.

400
00:28:44,793 --> 00:28:46,102
Want some water, Ciandrei?

401
00:28:46,102 --> 00:28:47,043
No, I’m good.

402
00:28:47,353 --> 00:28:47,979
Okay.

403
00:28:49,292 --> 00:28:50,877
You know, it’s kinda weird.

404
00:28:51,208 --> 00:28:53,169
You always call me by my full name.

405
00:28:56,196 --> 00:28:57,030
Shan.

406
00:29:02,452 --> 00:29:03,244
Much better.

407
00:29:05,789 --> 00:29:07,248
Where are you spending Christmas?

408
00:29:09,125 --> 00:29:10,121
Bataan.

409
00:29:11,211 --> 00:29:13,797
We’ll all get together, my
relatives on my dad’s side.

410
00:29:13,797 --> 00:29:14,422
You?

411
00:29:15,215 --> 00:29:16,132
I’ll just be in the condo.

412
00:29:16,800 --> 00:29:17,707
By yourself?

413
00:29:18,843 --> 00:29:19,969
It’s my Christmas tradition.

414
00:29:21,012 --> 00:29:23,598
Would you like to break that tradition?

415
00:29:24,891 --> 00:29:26,142
Come with us to Bataan.

416
00:29:26,351 --> 00:29:27,310
I’ll tell my mom.

417
00:29:28,436 --> 00:29:29,270
Are you sure?

418
00:29:29,270 --> 00:29:29,854
Of course.

419
00:29:29,854 --> 00:29:31,189
You’re going to bring
me to meet your parents?

420
00:29:31,189 --> 00:29:35,610
Yeah, my parents are nice,
and they’d like you to be there.

421
00:29:38,363 --> 00:29:39,322
Okay, sure.

422
00:29:39,697 --> 00:29:41,449
Let’s break my Christmas tradition.

423
00:29:58,758 --> 00:30:00,301
Have you booked your ticket yet?

424
00:30:01,928 --> 00:30:02,930
No.

425
00:30:03,179 --> 00:30:05,598
I have my own plans for
Christmas. I’m not coming.

426
00:30:09,352 --> 00:30:10,895
I can’t say I’m surprised.

427
00:30:12,063 --> 00:30:12,981
So what?

428
00:30:14,566 --> 00:30:16,150
You only asked for me here for that?

429
00:30:17,861 --> 00:30:18,778
I don’t think so.

430
00:30:23,199 --> 00:30:25,577
I talked with Mayor Villaflor.

431
00:30:26,786 --> 00:30:31,499
He mentioned that you and his son
do not get along at law school.

432
00:30:32,876 --> 00:30:33,793
And so?

433
00:30:34,878 --> 00:30:37,630
Why would I make friends
with the son of a crook?

434
00:30:38,798 --> 00:30:40,800
He’s a carbon copy of his father.

435
00:30:43,553 --> 00:30:44,429
Shan.

436
00:30:53,307 --> 00:30:54,850
Can you show some respect?

437
00:30:55,481 --> 00:30:56,649
The Mayor’s a friend of mine.

438
00:30:57,817 --> 00:31:00,028
I want to keep a
good relationship with him.

439
00:31:00,528 --> 00:31:02,822
He’s running for governor soon.

440
00:31:03,615 --> 00:31:06,951
So I want you to build
a good connnections with his son.

441
00:31:07,201 --> 00:31:08,102
Okay?

442
00:31:12,457 --> 00:31:13,875
What’s so funny?

443
00:31:14,812 --> 00:31:15,726
Nothing.

444
00:31:16,669 --> 00:31:18,404
I just realized that
people with the same

445
00:31:18,428 --> 00:31:20,381
attitudes get along
really well, don't they?

446
00:31:20,715 --> 00:31:22,508
Abusers, thieves, criminals—

447
00:31:22,508 --> 00:31:23,760
all in one group.

448
00:31:25,094 --> 00:31:28,514
Sorry, but I can’t be
friends with people like that.

449
00:31:29,432 --> 00:31:30,767
You can just talk amongst yourselves.

450
00:31:31,851 --> 00:31:33,937
I don’t want to catch your corrupt mindset.

451
00:31:34,979 --> 00:31:38,983
Fuck you! You’re really rude!

452
00:31:40,151 --> 00:31:43,947
Watch your mouth.
You haven’t done a single thing right!

453
00:31:44,322 --> 00:31:46,199
This is all I’m asking for,
and you still can’t do it!

454
00:31:46,199 --> 00:31:50,286
And I’ll do everything
I can to bring Miguel down.

455
00:31:50,954 --> 00:31:52,038
You’re such an idiot.

456
00:31:52,330 --> 00:31:53,873
You don’t know how it works!

457
00:31:54,457 --> 00:31:57,377
If you want to survive in
this world and make money—

458
00:31:57,543 --> 00:31:59,170
side with the ones in power!

459
00:31:59,170 --> 00:32:00,713
That’s where we differ!

460
00:32:01,255 --> 00:32:03,174
Because I side with the people.

461
00:32:03,466 --> 00:32:05,005
You can stay there with
those corrupt people.

462
00:32:05,029 --> 00:32:07,095
I don’t care what kind of
relationship you have with them.

463
00:32:07,261 --> 00:32:09,263
You guys can have
each other, okay?

464
00:32:10,515 --> 00:32:11,557
I don’t care about it.

465
00:32:11,891 --> 00:32:13,601
Because you don’t
mean anything to me at all.

466
00:32:15,937 --> 00:32:16,646
Shan!

467
00:32:32,161 --> 00:32:35,498
Gingerbread latte. Our seasonal drink.

468
00:32:35,498 --> 00:32:38,334
And you’re one of the
first people to taste it.

469
00:32:38,710 --> 00:32:40,044
Perks of being a VIP.

470
00:32:40,294 --> 00:32:41,129
VIP?

471
00:32:42,380 --> 00:32:43,339
VIP.

472
00:32:43,923 --> 00:32:46,759
My very important person.

473
00:32:55,768 --> 00:32:57,478
Wait, is that a bruise?

474
00:32:59,147 --> 00:33:00,148
What happened?

475
00:33:02,442 --> 00:33:02,859
It’s nothing.

476
00:33:02,859 --> 00:33:04,610
Don’t tell me your dad hurt you again.

477
00:33:05,653 --> 00:33:07,113
No, no, it’s nothing.

478
00:33:07,905 --> 00:33:10,950
Just an accident in the back.

479
00:33:10,950 --> 00:33:14,954
You know, some boxes fell on me and stuff.

480
00:33:14,954 --> 00:33:17,081
So, it’s nothing serious, don’t worry.

481
00:33:17,373 --> 00:33:19,292
I’m fine. It’s nothing.

482
00:33:19,751 --> 00:33:20,501
Are you sure?

483
00:33:20,501 --> 00:33:21,127
Yeah.

484
00:33:22,253 --> 00:33:24,881
Come on, try it. Don’t worry about me.

485
00:33:32,555 --> 00:33:33,556
- It’s delicious.
- How was it?

486
00:33:33,556 --> 00:33:35,141
Delicious, right? Told you.

487
00:33:35,475 --> 00:33:36,642
It’s not too sweet.

488
00:33:37,685 --> 00:33:38,603
Tastes like Christmas.

489
00:33:39,604 --> 00:33:40,688
Right?

490
00:33:49,447 --> 00:33:50,740
The University Christmas Party’s coming up.

491
00:33:52,492 --> 00:33:53,326
Are you guys going?

492
00:33:55,953 --> 00:33:58,539
You know, my last University
Christmas Party wasn’t fun.

493
00:33:59,165 --> 00:34:00,166
It wasn’t good.

494
00:34:01,125 --> 00:34:01,976
Why?

495
00:34:02,001 --> 00:34:03,586
I mean, if you don’t mind, what happened?

496
00:34:05,463 --> 00:34:08,800
I introduced my ex to my friends.

497
00:34:09,842 --> 00:34:10,968
They didn’t like him.

498
00:34:12,804 --> 00:34:14,597
It turned out badly.

499
00:34:15,473 --> 00:34:18,017
I have a bad feeling about that guy.
You’d better be careful.

500
00:34:18,017 --> 00:34:20,353
You never hear me say
anything about your men, Yanna.

501
00:34:20,353 --> 00:34:21,687
- What did you just say?
- Hey!

502
00:34:21,687 --> 00:34:22,396
- Yanna!
- Hey!

503
00:34:22,396 --> 00:34:26,025
Ke we’re not enemies
here. We’re your friends.

504
00:34:26,025 --> 00:34:27,212
Come on!

505
00:34:27,610 --> 00:34:28,611
Friends?

506
00:34:28,986 --> 00:34:30,238
It doesn’t feel that way anymore.

507
00:34:32,954 --> 00:34:35,016
We had a fight.

508
00:34:36,702 --> 00:34:38,454
I even defended my ex.

509
00:34:41,833 --> 00:34:43,668
And I wanted him to look good.

510
00:34:44,617 --> 00:34:50,874
Because if he didn’t get along with them,
my ex would blame me and hurt me.

511
00:34:55,304 --> 00:34:56,764
I’m sorry that happened.

512
00:34:59,684 --> 00:35:02,770
I think that was the
heaviest fight we’ve ever had.

513
00:35:04,522 --> 00:35:05,773
I cried so hard back then.

514
00:35:08,151 --> 00:35:12,238
I also said some things that weren’t nice.

515
00:35:12,655 --> 00:35:14,031
I don’t want that to happen again.

516
00:35:15,116 --> 00:35:18,119
I don’t want to fight with them anymore,
especially with Luna.

517
00:35:19,120 --> 00:35:22,707
I can’t believe I chose
that man over my friends.

518
00:35:27,003 --> 00:35:31,549
You know, Ke, there are
moments in life when...

519
00:35:32,049 --> 00:35:33,885
You simply have to
make a decision because...

520
00:35:34,802 --> 00:35:36,387
The situation demands it.

521
00:35:37,889 --> 00:35:39,557
It doesn’t make you a bad person.

522
00:35:41,642 --> 00:35:42,393
Right?

523
00:35:44,312 --> 00:35:45,188
Thank you.

524
00:35:46,355 --> 00:35:48,065
Well, I’m excited…

525
00:35:49,025 --> 00:35:51,360
to spend Christmas with you.

526
00:35:52,612 --> 00:35:53,529
Me, too.

527
00:35:58,326 --> 00:35:59,994
Try this, it’s good.

528
00:36:13,591 --> 00:36:14,800
Hi, come in.

529
00:36:14,884 --> 00:36:15,726
Hi.

530
00:36:18,930 --> 00:36:20,932
Welcome to our Bataan house!

531
00:36:21,474 --> 00:36:22,558
Nice house.

532
00:36:23,017 --> 00:36:24,518
It's big.

533
00:36:26,646 --> 00:36:29,582
Sorry. This is for your mom.

534
00:36:29,607 --> 00:36:30,942
Let me introduce you.

535
00:36:30,942 --> 00:36:34,111
Mommy! My friend’s here.

536
00:36:37,573 --> 00:36:38,115
Hello.

537
00:36:38,115 --> 00:36:38,824
- Hello.
- Oh.

538
00:36:38,824 --> 00:36:40,201
Wow, thank you.

539
00:36:40,451 --> 00:36:42,078
Thank you for inviting me.

540
00:36:42,495 --> 00:36:43,329
No problem.

541
00:36:43,329 --> 00:36:46,082
Mom, this is Ciandrei Lopez.
Shan, this is Mom.

542
00:36:46,249 --> 00:36:47,583
Is Dad still upstairs?

543
00:36:47,583 --> 00:36:48,626
He’s still upstairs.

544
00:36:49,794 --> 00:36:53,339
Are you perhaps related to Ciana Lopez?

545
00:36:55,216 --> 00:36:56,050
Yes, ma’am.

546
00:36:56,634 --> 00:36:57,760
She’s my mother.

547
00:36:59,470 --> 00:37:00,513
This is for you.

548
00:37:08,771 --> 00:37:09,438
Thank you.

549
00:37:09,438 --> 00:37:10,606
Have a seat.

550
00:37:11,107 --> 00:37:11,899
Thank you.

551
00:37:11,899 --> 00:37:13,276
Thank you.

552
00:37:14,151 --> 00:37:18,281
You know, we’re good friends with your mom.

553
00:37:19,240 --> 00:37:21,909
We’ve met before, you know.
You were still a kid.

554
00:37:22,285 --> 00:37:24,453
And you grew up so well.

555
00:37:24,914 --> 00:37:25,830
Thank you.

556
00:37:27,415 --> 00:37:29,500
You two really are soulmates.

557
00:37:29,625 --> 00:37:30,501
Ma, come on.

558
00:37:30,960 --> 00:37:31,752
Why?

559
00:37:32,128 --> 00:37:33,546
Aren’t you two in a relationship?

560
00:37:33,546 --> 00:37:35,840
No! We’re just friends.

561
00:37:38,406 --> 00:37:39,510
Okay.

562
00:37:40,011 --> 00:37:41,971
I’m sorry. I was just asking.

563
00:37:42,722 --> 00:37:47,226
But you know what, take your
time figuring things out, okay?

564
00:37:54,066 --> 00:37:55,443
Thank you.

565
00:37:57,278 --> 00:37:59,030
It’s a pleasure to meet you, sir.

566
00:37:59,030 --> 00:38:02,283
Kierra speaks of you often,
and I have seen your work.

567
00:38:02,658 --> 00:38:03,534
They’re so great.

568
00:38:03,534 --> 00:38:05,703
Really? Thanks.

569
00:38:07,997 --> 00:38:08,998
Just call me Uncle.

570
00:38:09,582 --> 00:38:13,210
It feels strange to me that you call
me "sir." It’s as if you were my student.

571
00:38:15,171 --> 00:38:19,508
Well, these are some of my earlier works.

572
00:38:21,344 --> 00:38:22,470
And that—

573
00:38:24,353 --> 00:38:26,647
Kierra helped me paint.

574
00:38:27,266 --> 00:38:33,981
She was about seven years old back then,
and this story has a funny backstory.

575
00:38:34,273 --> 00:38:34,982
Really?

576
00:38:34,982 --> 00:38:35,775
Yeah.

577
00:38:35,775 --> 00:38:40,738
When Kierra was little,
she loved drawing all sorts of things.

578
00:38:40,738 --> 00:38:45,368
I think when I was working on this,
she felt like something was missing.

579
00:38:45,368 --> 00:38:48,120
It’s a dark concept, as you can see.

580
00:38:48,329 --> 00:38:49,789
So she added these.

581
00:38:49,789 --> 00:38:52,291
Rainbows around it and unicorns.

582
00:38:53,501 --> 00:39:00,216
But instead of getting angry,
I took it as our first collaboration.

583
00:39:01,258 --> 00:39:04,595
Because I recognized
that to her, it’s still art.

584
00:39:05,846 --> 00:39:09,308
And I didn’t want to
limit Kierra’s imagination.

585
00:39:11,435 --> 00:39:13,354
You’re such a great father, Uncle.

586
00:39:13,896 --> 00:39:16,899
It’s no surprise to me that Kierra is
the way she is. It’s because of you, too.

587
00:39:17,566 --> 00:39:21,070
I heard my name. Are you
talking about me, Daddy?

588
00:39:21,570 --> 00:39:24,281
Don’t tell him too many
things about me, okay?

589
00:39:24,281 --> 00:39:26,784
I’m just showing him my paintings.

590
00:39:27,284 --> 00:39:29,286
And my dad’s bragging now.

591
00:39:29,286 --> 00:39:30,663
And our painting, too.

592
00:39:31,622 --> 00:39:33,082
Daddy, come on.

593
00:39:33,666 --> 00:39:34,542
What—

594
00:39:34,542 --> 00:39:35,418
It’s nice.

595
00:39:35,418 --> 00:39:37,920
- Everything’s nice.
- Shan needs to rest, you know?

596
00:39:39,255 --> 00:39:42,007
Well, that’s right.
You should get some rest first.

597
00:39:42,174 --> 00:39:45,970
We’ll call you later when
we’re about to leave.

598
00:39:45,970 --> 00:39:47,304
We’ll go to the resort later.

599
00:39:47,680 --> 00:39:48,431
- Okay, Uncle.
- Sure.

600
00:39:48,431 --> 00:39:49,723
- All right?
- Thank you.

601
00:39:51,559 --> 00:39:52,560
See you later.

602
00:39:52,726 --> 00:39:53,477
Well?

603
00:39:53,853 --> 00:39:57,565
Let’s take your things to the
guest room so you can rest for a while.

604
00:39:59,024 --> 00:40:00,651
I’m actually not tired.

605
00:40:01,569 --> 00:40:03,863
Do you want to watch
a movie? I brought my laptop.

606
00:40:04,155 --> 00:40:05,948
Sure. Can we watch a romantic comedy?

607
00:40:06,031 --> 00:40:07,408
Sure. Let’s go?

608
00:40:07,450 --> 00:40:08,330
Come on.

609
00:40:16,709 --> 00:40:20,129
I said romantic comedy.
This is not a romantic comedy.

610
00:40:20,561 --> 00:40:24,732
I said I don’t want to watch one
where they don’t end up together.

611
00:40:26,469 --> 00:40:28,262
Sorry. Don’t cry.

612
00:40:28,554 --> 00:40:32,725
There are still a lot of...
there are still lessons in it, though.

613
00:40:33,225 --> 00:40:36,395
Besides, if you ask me, I’d prefer
it if they didn’t end up together.

614
00:40:36,395 --> 00:40:38,022
’Cause they’re better
off without each other.

615
00:40:38,481 --> 00:40:41,442
And who knows, maybe
they’re together in real life.

616
00:40:42,443 --> 00:40:46,071
That rarely happens.
Especially in show business.

617
00:40:46,405 --> 00:40:48,365
But I know someone, my friend...

618
00:40:51,243 --> 00:40:52,328
Which friend?

619
00:40:52,328 --> 00:40:53,179
Nothing.

620
00:40:54,356 --> 00:40:57,773
No fair, you’re so stingy
with gossip. Just spill it.

621
00:40:58,083 --> 00:41:02,296
You know that if Luna hears
you say that, she’ll call you a gossip.

622
00:41:07,927 --> 00:41:10,012
Your bangs are getting kind of long.

623
00:41:10,155 --> 00:41:10,947
Yeah, they are.

624
00:41:11,180 --> 00:41:12,473
I can barely see your eyes.

625
00:41:12,556 --> 00:41:15,017
I forgot to trim them.
They’re bothering my eyes.

626
00:41:16,560 --> 00:41:18,148
Do you want me to cut them for you?

627
00:41:18,270 --> 00:41:19,304
You know how?

628
00:41:19,813 --> 00:41:20,606
Trust me.

629
00:41:21,315 --> 00:41:22,399
Wait, I have scissors.

630
00:41:32,034 --> 00:41:33,577
What if they come out uneven?

631
00:41:33,953 --> 00:41:34,870
Trust me.

632
00:41:35,162 --> 00:41:36,625
Come on, hurry, sit here.

633
00:41:42,503 --> 00:41:43,212
Hey!

634
00:41:43,587 --> 00:41:44,672
You’re making me nervous.

635
00:41:44,672 --> 00:41:46,048
Just make sure you do it right.

636
00:41:46,090 --> 00:41:47,174
I’ve got you.

637
00:41:47,341 --> 00:41:49,468
Wait, I’m concentrating, I need to focus.

638
00:41:49,468 --> 00:41:50,970
Let me concentrate. Okay?

639
00:42:18,455 --> 00:42:19,581
Can I see?

640
00:42:21,834 --> 00:42:22,960
There, go check.

641
00:42:26,171 --> 00:42:30,759
Oh, they’re even. Not bad.

642
00:42:30,759 --> 00:42:32,970
Right? There you go.

643
00:42:34,054 --> 00:42:35,431
I can see your eyes more now.

644
00:42:37,516 --> 00:42:38,350
It’s pretty.

645
00:42:45,608 --> 00:42:46,483
Thank you.

646
00:43:35,783 --> 00:43:37,993
Fine, I’ll just take this. It looks good.

647
00:43:39,119 --> 00:43:40,245
- Oh.
- Don’t touch that.

648
00:43:40,245 --> 00:43:40,954
Why?

649
00:43:42,956 --> 00:43:43,957
That’s Kierra’s.

650
00:43:47,795 --> 00:43:48,420
Hey.

651
00:43:50,255 --> 00:43:52,007
Take good care of my cousin, okay?

652
00:43:53,884 --> 00:43:55,219
She’s been through a lot.

653
00:43:55,427 --> 00:43:57,888
So please, be kind to her.

654
00:43:59,390 --> 00:44:00,557
I’ll take care of her.

655
00:44:01,350 --> 00:44:02,434
I promise.

656
00:44:03,761 --> 00:44:06,370
And I’m not even going
to tell you not to hurt her,

657
00:44:06,403 --> 00:44:09,274
because you know who you’d
be messing with if you did.

658
00:44:09,566 --> 00:44:10,067
I know.

659
00:44:10,067 --> 00:44:12,027
Mhmm. You should.

660
00:44:12,027 --> 00:44:13,237
So, is this okay? Is it fine now?

661
00:44:13,237 --> 00:44:14,238
Yeah, that’s okay.

662
00:44:16,448 --> 00:44:18,033
My food still tastes better, though.

663
00:44:18,033 --> 00:44:18,992
You can have that.

664
00:44:19,368 --> 00:44:21,120
Well, let me try it.

665
00:44:23,831 --> 00:44:24,873
How is it?

666
00:44:26,792 --> 00:44:27,960
No, it’s not good.

667
00:44:28,460 --> 00:44:30,629
Mine’s still better.

668
00:44:44,268 --> 00:44:48,105
- Merry Christmas!
- Oh! Thank you. Wow.

669
00:44:48,105 --> 00:44:51,150
Nice meeting you, Ke’s boyfriend.

670
00:44:51,150 --> 00:44:52,568
Friend, Uncle. Just a friend.

671
00:44:52,901 --> 00:44:55,654
Weren't you always following him around?
You always went after him everywhere.

672
00:44:55,654 --> 00:44:58,115
That’s why he was annoyed with you—
because you were very naughty.

673
00:44:58,741 --> 00:44:59,800
Really, Auntie?

674
00:44:59,825 --> 00:45:01,160
Oh, look at her, she has a crush on me.

675
00:45:01,160 --> 00:45:03,078
One, two, three.

676
00:45:03,954 --> 00:45:05,456
Theo, come here.

677
00:45:05,605 --> 00:45:07,106
You’re the—

678
00:45:08,333 --> 00:45:10,085
You’re the barista from the coffee shop.

679
00:45:11,837 --> 00:45:13,088
Your coffee there is so good.

680
00:45:13,839 --> 00:45:14,757
Thank you.

681
00:45:15,549 --> 00:45:17,176
Come back anytime, my treat.

682
00:45:19,386 --> 00:45:23,056
You look so happy. It’s so obvious.

683
00:45:27,144 --> 00:45:29,396
Aren’t you jealous of him?

684
00:45:30,773 --> 00:45:31,398
Huh?

685
00:45:31,802 --> 00:45:33,262
You’re going to stop hanging out with them.

686
00:45:34,026 --> 00:45:36,652
And you’re not going to see
them anymore. Do you understand?

687
00:45:36,920 --> 00:45:38,589
You should just drink.

688
00:45:38,614 --> 00:45:39,907
Don’t get annoyed.

689
00:45:39,907 --> 00:45:41,116
Are you jealous?
